\par b- Ministry of Education: Chemical Substances intended for educational and research institutions.
\par c- Saudi Food and Drug Authority: Chemical precur
sors used in the manufacture of narcotic drugs and psychotropic substances; other Chemical Substances used in the preparation or manufacture of food and drugs; pesticides relating to public health; cosmetics; medical products; and Chemical Substances requ
ired by the health sector, including non-radioactive reagents.
\par d- Ministry of Environment, Water and Agriculture (the Competent Environmental Centre):
\par 1- Chemical Substances used in the preparation or manufacture of agricultural pesticides, soil conditioners and fertilisers, and Chemical Substances required by agricultural research centres.
\par 2- Chemical Substances used in water and wastewater treatment and the plants designated therefor, and Chemical Substances required by water and wastewater laboratories and research centres.
\par 3- Chemical substances restricted pursuant to international conventions and treaties ratified by the Kingdom in the environmental field, without prejudice to the competences of the other relevant authorities.
\par e- Minist
